    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66018.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Again, your government wanting to drive out anyone who will not meet their needs. And, you know, just to put it in perspective, people talk about a slippery slope. Well, let's talk about one. We get the all these back doors and these back doors are mandated. Then that takes care of national security, a terrorist. Next thing you know, of course, it's a drug bust. We had the the district attorney from new york who said he needed it for all of his drug cases Well, now the next thing we get into is a disgruntled ex-wife in a child custody case. Why can't they use it? No real difference between civil rights and criminal rights. And you keep going down to where it's simply a lawsuit between the two of us and I get to discover everything. Where do we stop in your ability to be private? You know, our founding fathers assumed that five people went into a room and they had a private discussion. In this day and age, what the courts are trying to be asked is, will you take away that right so that because you go in the room and there's a TV in the room, there's an echo in the room, well then why can't we listen to you?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Backdoors in technology are being mandated by authorities.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Privacy rights would be eroded if governments can monitor private communications under various pretexts.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Your government wants to drive out individuals who do not meet its needs.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Mandated backdoors initially serve national security and counter-terrorism purposes.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Backdoor access could extend to civil matters like child custody disputes involving a disgruntled ex-wife.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The Founding Fathers believed that private conversations among five people in a room were inherently protected.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Backdoors have already been used for drug enforcement cases.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
